--- body ---
## Context

Child of tracking ticket 0251 (Option A ratified: `/hunt` is the single
execution core every path invokes). Concrete bug found in the imagine
pass: `skills/hunt/SKILL.md` step 3 requires the worktree basename to be
exactly `t$ARGUMENTS`, but `Agent(isolation:"worktree")` names its
worktrees `agent-<id>`. A raid execute agent invoking `Skill(hunt)`
therefore fails the name check and re-attempts `EnterWorktree`, which
refuses from inside a worktree session — an error, though the agent's
isolation is in fact correct.

Scope note: this is one narrow instance of worktree ownership; the
broader ownership audit belongs to ticket 0252 — do not absorb it.

## Relevant files
- `skills/hunt/SKILL.md` — step 3, ~line 26-35
- `docs/imagine-0251-entry-points-2026-07-12.md` — design note, Q4 answer
- `scripts/beat.py` (~line 1219) — the headless invocation pattern to
  reference

## Actions
1. Generalize the ownership predicate in step 3: a worktree is OWNED when
   its basename is `t$ARGUMENTS` OR it was created by the spawner for
   this agent (an `agent-*` worktree the agent session started in, with a
   clean tree). A shared or `explore-*` worktree hosting a live session
   remains NOT owned — keep the 2026-06-11 incident rationale.
2. Treat an `EnterWorktree` "already in a worktree" rejection in a
   spawned-agent context as isolation-confirmed rather than an error,
   per the design note.
3. Add one sentence pointing ad hoc orchestrators at the beat.py
   headless pattern (`claude -p "/hunt <id>"`) instead of hand-typed
   contracts.

## Test
- Skills hygiene test asserting step 3 accepts the `agent-*` ownership
  case (greppable predicate text) and still forbids `explore-*`/shared
  worktrees.

## Verification
- [ ] A `Skill(hunt)` invocation from an `Agent(isolation:"worktree")`
      context passes step 3 without a spurious EnterWorktree attempt
- [ ] The 2026-06-11 shared-worktree protection is intact

## Invariants
- Interactive `/hunt` behavior unchanged (still creates/enters `t<id>`)
- No new entry point

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Ownership predicate generalized as above
- [ ] Rejection-as-confirmation branch documented in step 3
- [ ] beat.py headless pointer sentence added
- [ ] `make check` passes
